Muslim Ajuran Empire declared independence (economic independence) from **Portugal** by defying their Indian Ocean trade monopoly. Muslims were expelled from Portugal during the **Christian Reconquista** (when Portugal established itself as an independent kingdom in 1139). \n\nThat Dam is located in **Vientiane, Laos**, and the natural boundary/cross-border connection to **Myanmar** (Thailand's western neighbor) is where the Toungoo Dynasty \"defeated the Portuguese in 1613 and Siam in 1614.\"\n\nThus: Muslims were expelled from Portugal during the **Reconquista**, and later Portuguese were defeated/expelled from Myanmar in 1613 by the Toungoo Dynasty.\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_21bd83b40ffeJ2FaC6b9qOjjsX","model":{"modelID":"qwen35-9b","providerID":"local"},"truncated":false},"title":"Answer the multi-hop research question","time":{"start":1777649304760,"end":1777649377302}}}}
